{"url":"/distro/installer-reference","slug":"installer-reference","collection":"distro","group":"Architecture","title":"Installer reference","description":"The install_core API, palm-install, the configuration files an installed system honours, the i18n library and the live image.","toc":[{"id":"what-a-person-does","title":"What a person does","depth":2},{"id":"the-pieces","title":"The pieces","depth":2},{"id":"install_core-api","title":"install_core API","depth":2},{"id":"palm-install","title":"palm-install","depth":2},{"id":"system-configuration-files-the-installed-system-honours","title":"System configuration files the installed system honours","depth":2},{"id":"i18n-library-appskiti18nodin","title":"i18n library (apps/kit/i18n.odin)","depth":2},{"id":"live-image-distrolive","title":"Live image (distro/live/)","depth":2}],"source":{"path":"distro/INSTALLER.md","edit":"https://github.com/alexisbcz/palmy/edit/main/distro/INSTALLER.md","view":"https://github.com/alexisbcz/palmy/blob/main/distro/INSTALLER.md","generated":[]},"updated":"2026-10-19","hast":["#root",0,["p",0,"The installer's interfaces and behaviour. They are in addition to\n",["code",0,"CONTRACT.md"],". This file started as the contract the pieces were built\nagainst. It now describes what was built, and it remains the reference. Where\nthe build differs from the original contract, the text says so (\"",["em",0,"Built:"],"\").\nEach area's reasons are in ",["code",0,"distro/notes/<area>.md"],". How to use the installer,\nand what was verified in QEMU, is under ",["em",0,"Installing"]," in ",["code",0,"README.md"],"."],"\n",["h2",{"id":"what-a-person-does"},"What a person does"],"\n",["p",0,"Boot ",["code",0,"distro/out/palmframe-live.iso"]," in QEMU or from a USB stick. The ISO\nboots under UEFI and under BIOS (limine's CD images plus ",["code",0,"limine bios-install"],"\nfor hybrid USB boot). The live system runs entirely from RAM. It starts\nstraight into the graphical installer, which is ",["code",0,"wm --drm --kiosk --exec installer"]," as root, run through a live-only palm-init service. A root shell\nis on the serial console. The installer has eight steps, shown in a rail:"],"\n",["ol",0,"\n",["li",0,["strong",0,"Language."]," The UI switches immediately. The choices are English,\nFrançais, Deutsch, Español, العربية (right to left) and 日本語. Japanese\nis offered only when a CJK font is installed; otherwise it is listed as\nunavailable rather than drawn as tofu. The live system ships a CJK font subset,\nso Japanese is offered there. Choosing a language also preselects a\nkeyboard layout and a time zone until the person picks those."],"\n",["li",0,["strong",0,"Keyboard."]," A layout and variant from xkeyboard-config's ",["code",0,"base.lst"],",\nwith a test field. The compositor switches layout live."],"\n",["li",0,["strong",0,"Time zone."]," A region and city from tzdata's ",["code",0,"zone1970.tab"],", searchable,\nwith the local time shown."],"\n",["li",0,["strong",0,"Disk."]," Every block device from ",["code",0,"/sys/block"],", with size and model.\n",["em",0,"Erase the whole disk"]," (GPT: 512 MiB ESP and an ext4 root) is the only\nmode, stated plainly, and needs an explicit confirmation naming the\ndevice. In the confirmation dialog Cancel has the focus."],"\n",["li",0,["strong",0,"Account."]," Full name, user name, password (twice) and hostname. The root\npassword is the same as the user's unless changed."],"\n",["li",0,["strong",0,"Summary"],", then ",["strong",0,"Install"],": progress with the current step, and a log\nview."],"\n",["li",0,["strong",0,"Done"],", then ",["strong",0,"Restart"],"."],"\n"],"\n",["p",0,["em",0,"Built:"]," the rail counts Summary and Install as separate steps, so the GUI\nshows eight steps. The disk step also offers a swap file. An installed\ndisk boots under UEFI and under a BIOS (see ",["em",0,"Bootloader"],")."],"\n",["h2",{"id":"the-pieces"},"The pieces"],"\n",["table",0,"\n",["thead",0,"\n",["tr",0,"\n",["th",0,"piece"]